        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Haemoglobin is made of two α‑globin chains and two β‑globin chains.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 18
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A person may have a mutation in the gene coding for β‑globin. This is due to a base substitution and leads to the production of abnormal β‑globin and therefore abnormal haemoglobin.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 18
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A person who is homozygous for the mutant allele will have a condition called sickle cell anaemia.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 18
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Outline the phenotypic effects of having abnormal haemoglobin in a person with sickle cell anaemia.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "16.2(6)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>four</i></b><i> from: </i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "haemoglobin less soluble <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "(if oxygen concentration decreases) haemoglobin molecules, stick together / form long fibres <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "red blood cells, pulled out of shape / become sickle shaped <b>; </b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "blood poor at transporting oxygen <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "text": "(so) less oxygen getting to, cells / tissues / organs <b>;</b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 6,
              "text": "red blood cells may, get stuck in / block, capillaries / vessels <b>; </b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 7,
              "text": "pain / sickle cell crisis / fatigue <b>; </b>"
            }
          ],
          "source": {
            "ms": 16
          },
          "marks": 4
        },
        "er": [
          "er.q7.a"
        ],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "The altered haemoglobin protein and the red blood cell containing it are different structures. Protein aggregation changes the cell shape and can obstruct small vessels, so explain oxygen delivery and circulation as linked consequences.",
              "refs": [
                "ms:a#1",
                "ms:a#2",
                "ms:a#3",
                "ms:a#4",
                "ms:a#5",
                "ms:a#6",
                "ms:a#7",
                "syllabus:16.2(6)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Start with altered haemoglobin properties.",
            "Trace aggregation to red-cell shape and vessel blockage.",
            "Relate these changes to reduced oxygen delivery and symptoms."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": []
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 18
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<b>Hb<sup>A</sup></b> is the allele coding for normal β‑globin.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 18
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<b>Hb<sup>S</sup></b> is the allele coding for abnormal β‑globin.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 18
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The alleles are codominant.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "parts": [
          {
